In this proof of concept, the address 0xbEEF, which is not authorised, can successfully call flashLoan and receive a flash loan amount of 10 ether without any checks or restrictions.
## Tools Used
Manual review & foundry test.
## Recommended Mitigation Steps

To mitigate this vulnerability, implement an access control mechanism to restrict the flashLoan function to only authorised addresses or contracts. 

This can be achieved by integrating role-based access control or owner checks.

Here’s a suggested implementation using OpenZeppelin’s AccessControl:
```sol
    function flashLoan(
        IERC3156FlashBorrower receiver,
        address token,
        uint256 amount,
        bytes calldata data
    ) external override nonReentrant onlyRole(FLASHLOANER_ROLE) returns (bool) {
```

Unauthorised access to flash loan functions can result in significant financial harm to the protocol and its users, especially if the vulnerability is exploited in a high-volume trading environment.


